@startuml iceberg-write-path
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam component {
  BorderColor #534AB7
  BackgroundColor #EEEDFE
  FontColor #26215C
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #0F6E56
  BackgroundColor #E1F5EE
  FontColor #04342C
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #888780
  BackgroundColor #F1EFE8
  FontColor #2C2C2A
}

title labukDB — Iceberg Write Path (labukdb-format-iceberg)\nCopyright 2026 Afzal and lakehouse-flight contributors — Apache 2.0

database "Iceberg table\n(metadata/ + Parquet)" as IT #9FE1CB

[IcebergTableCreator\n(path-based via HadoopTables.create,\nor catalog-based via Catalog.createTable;\nidentity-only partitioning)] as ITCR
[ArrowToIcebergSchema\n(Arrow Schema -> org.apache.iceberg.Schema;\nStruct/Map get their own field IDs\nvia one running counter)] as AIS
[IcebergDataFileWriter\n(write a new Parquet file + build\nthe matching DataFile -- shared by\nappendBatch and IcebergTableMerger)] as IDFW

[IcebergTableWriter\n(append-only; Table.newAppend()\nretries OCC conflicts internally --\nno hand-built retry loop needed)] as ITW
[IcebergTableMerger\n(upsert/MERGE by key; commits via\nTable.newOverwrite())] as ITMRG
[PartitionRowMerger\n(shared with Delta's TableMerger --\nsame merge-by-key semantics,\nnot a second independently-evolving copy)] as PRM
[IcebergCompactor\n(bin-pack small files; commits via\nTable.newRewrite() -- the real\nnon-data-changing commit type,\nconfirmed via javap, not newOverwrite())] as ICOMP
[IcebergVacuum\n(thin wrapper over Iceberg's own\nnative Table.expireSnapshots())] as IVAC

[DynamoDbLockManager\n(implements Iceberg's own\nLockManager extension point --\nlease-based acquire/release)] as IDDBL
[IcebergLockManagerConfig\n(opt-in: sets Configuration's\n"lock-impl" property when\nICEBERG_LOCK_DYNAMODB_TABLE is set)] as ILMC
[RemoteWriteSafetyWarning\n(shared with Delta's write path)] as RWSW

[IcebergRestConfiguration\n(ICEBERG_REST_* env vars -> RESTCatalog)] as IRC
[IcebergRestLocation\n(icebergrest://ns.table parsing)] as IRL

ITCR --> AIS : build Iceberg schema
ITCR --> IT : create table (version 0)
ITCR ..> ITW : table immediately usable\nby existing, unmodified writer

ITW --> IT : commit via iceberg-core\n(Table.newAppend)
ITW --> IDFW : appendBatch() delegates\nwrite+build-DataFile step
ITW ..> ILMC : construction --\napplyIfConfigured(conf)
ITW ..> RWSW : construction --\nwarns if remote + no lock

ITMRG --> IDFW : write new merged file\n+ build DataFile
ITMRG --> PRM : reuses core's exact\nsame merge-by-key semantics
ICOMP --> IDFW : write new merged file\n+ build DataFile
ICOMP --> PRM : combineFiles() only --\nno merge-by-key needed
IVAC --> IDFW : locationOf() -- resolve an\nexpired DataFile's path for deletion
IVAC --> IT : table.expireSnapshots()

ILMC ..> IDDBL : sets Configuration's\n"lock-impl" property
IRC ..> ITW : Catalog passed to\nnew (Catalog, TableIdentifier) ctor

note right of ITW
  <b>CONFIRMED BROKEN</b> under genuine
  concurrent writers on real MinIO, root
  cause traced into iceberg-core's own
  HadoopTableOperations.renameToFinal:
  default LockManager (InMemoryLockManager)
  is a plain HashMap per-JVM -- zero
  protection across separate processes --
  then fs.rename() (copy+delete on S3A,
  not atomic) lets every racing writer
  "succeed" with no conflict detected.
  MERGE confirmed separately broken too
  (4 of 8 concurrent inserts lost).

  With lock (DynamoDbLockManager):
  <b>done, live-verified</b> -- append AND
  MERGE both pass with it engaged. Full
  write lifecycle (create -> append ->
  merge -> compact -> vacuum) proven
  end-to-end against real MinIO.
end note

note bottom of IDDBL
  Same ResourceInUseException bootstrap
  race fixed here as Delta's
  DynamoDbLockProvider -- found via THIS
  class's own 8-separate-process test
  first, then confirmed Delta's lock had
  the identical unprotected createTable
  call. Scope deliberately smaller than
  Delta's lock: a lease-based steal, not
  a crash-recovery system -- Iceberg's own
  SnapshotProducer.commit() retry loop
  already handles everything else.
end note

note bottom of IRC
  <b>REST catalog + real MinIO, full data
  round trip: done, live-verified</b> (this
  session) -- the one gap
  IcebergRestConfiguration's own earlier
  javadoc had flagged as environment-
  blocked. Solved with CATALOG_WAREHOUSE=
  s3a://... (not s3://) so the REST
  server's reported locations resolve
  against this project's own
  MinioConfiguration. Real live-only
  issues found + fixed along the way:
  container DNS resolving the MinIO
  hostname to its own loopback (fixed via
  --add-host host-gateway), and the
  container's JVM not trusting a local
  mkcert dev cert (fixed via keytool,
  run as root).
end note

@enduml
